{{Term/Store|Meat|Meats|Series, TLoZ, TP, TPHD, BotW, TotK, EoW, HWL, HWDE, AoC|plural}} are a recurring class of [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="Encyclopedia">{{Cite Book|quote= |book= E |publisher= |page= 74 {{Exp Game|TLoZ, TP}}}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Koko donned her apron and prepared to dish up a tough meat-stuffed pumpkin for her exhausted father, Dorian.<br/><br/>Without any {{Color BotW|Red|meat}}, though, this chef's in a bind. She needs a skilled hunter to procure some {{Color BotW|Red|meat}} for her.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Raw Meat}}<br/>Meat obtained from animals in plains and forests. You can eat it raw, but cooking it will make it more delicious and nutritious.|Inventory|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|{{Color EoW|Pink|Meat}}}}<br/>A large hunk of bone-in meat that has been roasted to glistening. Its dripping juices entice certain monsters.|Notebook|EoW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Meat|Dining Room|HWL}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Meat|Dining Room|HWDE}}</ref>{{Name Ref|AoC}}

==Location and Uses==
==={{TLoZ|-}}===
{{Main|Bait}}
{{Stub|TLoZ}}

==={{TP|-}}===
Meats can be seen behind the counter at [[Telma's Bar]]. [[Telma]] also serves processed Meats to her customers, such as ham.<ref name="Encyclopedia"/>

==={{BotW|-}}===
In {{BotW}}, Meats can be obtained by killing [[Creature]]s. The quality and type of Meat is dependent on what kind of Creature has been killed. For example, mammals will drop [[Raw Meat]]s, [[Raw Prime Meat]]s, and [[Raw Gourmet Meat]]s when they have been defeated, while [[Bird]]s drop [[Raw Bird Thigh]]s, [[Raw Bird Drumstick]]s, and [[Raw Whole Bird]]s.

All Meats can be turned into both [[Roasted Food]] and [[Frozen Food]]. In addition to this, several [[Recipe]]s require Meats as [[Cooking]] [[Ingredient]]s. [[Creamy Meat Soup]], [[Glazed Meat]], a [[Meat-Stuffed Pumpkin]], a [[Meat and Mushroom Skewer]], [[Meat Pie]], a [[Meat Skewer]], and [[Copious Meat Skewers]], [[Meaty Rice Balls]], [[Monster Stew]], [[Pepper Steak]], [[Steamed Meat]] can use any type of Meat when Cooking them. Recipes that use a specific type of Meat are a [[Gourmet Meat and Rice Bowl]], [[Gourmet Meat and Seafood Fry]], [[Gourmet Meat Curry]], [[Gourmet Meat Stew]], [[Gourmet Poultry Pilaf]], a [[Gourmet Spiced Meat Skewer]], a [[Meat and Rice Bowl]], [[Meat and Seafood Fry]], [[Meat Curry]], [[Meat Stew]], [[Poultry Curry]], [[Poultry Pilaf]], a [[Prime Meat and Rice Bowl]], [[Prime Meat and Seafood Fry]], [[Prime Meat Curry]], [[Prime Meat Stew]], [[Prime Poultry Curry]], [[Prime Poultry Pilaf]], a [[Prime Spiced Meat Skewer]], [[Salt-Grilled Gourmet Meat]], [[Salt-Grilled Meat]], [[Salt-Grilled Prime Meat]], and a [[Spiced Meat Skewer]]

